<h2 class="font-headline-md text-headline-md text-primary mb-4">Types of Bacterial Mouth Infections</h2>
</div>
<div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Acute Apical Abscess</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">Pus formation at the tip of a tooth root from bacterial invasion of the dental pulp. Causes throbbing pain, bite sensitivity, and often facial swelling. <a href="dental-abscess-treatment-hyderabad.php" class="text-secondary underline hover:text-primary">Dental abscess treatment</a> covers this in detail.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Acute Periodontal Abscess</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">Bacterial infection of an existing periodontal (gum) pocket — causes a gumboil, pus discharge, gum tenderness, and tooth mobility. Often triggered by a foreign body or food impaction.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Pericoronitis</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">Bacterial infection around a partially erupted impacted tooth — most commonly a lower wisdom tooth. Causes gum swelling, pain when swallowing, and can spread to facial spaces.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Necrotizing Ulcerative Gingivitis</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">Painful necrotizing bacterial infection of the gums — causes bleeding gums, gray foul-smelling tissue, and crater-like ulcers between teeth. Requires urgent debridement and antibiotics.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Space Infection</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">Oral bacteria spreading from a tooth into facial spaces (buccal, submasseteric, submandibular). Creates significant facial swelling and risk of airway compromise. <a href="tooth-infection-swelling-treatment-hyderabad.php" class="text-secondary underline hover:text-primary">Tooth infection swelling</a> page has more detail.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Salivary Gland Infection</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">Bacterial infection of the parotid or submandibular salivary glands — often from a blocked duct. Causes painful cheek or under-jaw swelling with pus discharge from the gland opening.</p></div>
